  "reply_construction_scope": [
    "Logical replies are freshly constructed codec inputs, not daemon-produced replies or proof of range removal, execution, staging, durability, caps, ENOENT/EOPNOTSUPP semantics, erasure pool behavior or server limits.",
    "The public MOSDOpReply constructor keeps the request WRITE/RETURNVEC mode bits and replaces only ONDISK/ONNVRAM/ACK with the explicit acktype: ONDISK for success and failok, ACK|ONDISK for enoent and eopnotsupp.",
    "ACK|ONDISK on the refused vectors follows pinned PrimaryLogPG.cc: a failed do_osd_ops in a may_write vector sets update_log_only (prepare_transaction 8991-8998) and execute_ctx adds ACK|ONDISK before record_write_error (4366).",
    "The OMAPRMKEYRANGE handler (PrimaryLogPG.cc 8067-8093) checks !pool.info.supports_omap() first (EOPNOTSUPP, 8069-8072; osd_types.h 1787-1789 is false only for erasure pools) and then !obs.exists or whiteout (ENOENT, 8076-8079). The eopnotsupp vector is only the logical erasure-pool refusal shape; no erasure pool was exercised.",
    "Per-op results follow pinned do_osd_ops (8205-8213): enoent and eopnotsupp are a single OMAPRMKEYRANGE(61, 62) with aggregate and per-op -2 or -95; failok is OMAPRMKEYRANGE(61, 62, FAILOK) -2 then SETVALS 0 with aggregate 0.",
    "Every reply carries the logical set_reply_versions(11'20, 19) used by earlier native vectors. A live -ENOENT write refusal additionally calls set_enoent_reply_versions(info.last_update, info.last_user_version) (PrimaryLogPG.cc 4362-4364); those live version values are not represented here.",
    "Public claim_ops supplies input-union echoes and explicit results. Native merge_osd_op_vector_out_data independently derives payload_len 0 for every operation; OMAPRMKEYRANGE and SETVALS return no output."
  ],
